tonic 0.14.6 server: max_connection_age sends the GOAWAY, grace is counted
after it, the age is jittered (gRFC A9)

Applied by scripts/fetch-upstream.sh to the tonic-0.14.6 crate from crates.io
(paths relative to the crate root; upstream it is tonic/src/...). otap-rs
builds against it through `[patch.crates-io]`; patches/0004 relies on it.

`Server::max_connection_age` / `max_connection_age_grace` in 0.14.6:

1. With a grace, no GOAWAY is ever sent: connection_timeout_future sleeps
   age + grace and then drops the connection, so clients keep starting RPCs
   on it until it is cut under them.
   Upstream: open PR grpc/grpc-rust#2877 (same approach as here).
2. Without a grace, the completed connection_timeout_future is polled again
   on the next loop iteration: panic "`async fn` resumed after completion",
   which kills the connection task and its in-flight RPCs.
   Upstream: issue #2522, fixed by #2780 (wrap it in Fuse), merged
   2026-07-30, not in a release yet (0.14.6 is the latest).
3. No per-connection jitter, which gRFC A9 requires (+/-10%), so
   connections accepted together are recycled together. Not reported.

Fix: two fused timers per connection. At the (jittered) age: debug log,
hyper's graceful_shutdown (for HTTP/2, GOAWAY last-stream-id 2^31-1 + PING,
then the real last id; in-flight streams continue), and start the grace
timer; when that fires, drop the connection. Jitter: age x [0.9, 1.1) from
std's RandomState (no new dependency); an age too large to scale is kept.

Tests (src/transport/server/mod.rs, paused time, one HTTP/2 connection over
tokio::io::duplex, no Channel reconnects): raw-frame two-step GOAWAY at the
jittered age with and without a grace; in-flight call completes within the
grace while a new one is refused with GOAWAY/NO_ERROR, and the connection
closes as soon as it is done; a call longer than the grace is cut at age +
grace; no grace + busy connection does not panic; no age keeps the
connection (grace alone is inert); jitter bounds. On unpatched 0.14.6 three
of them fail (no GOAWAY with a grace; new call accepted after the age;
`async fn` resumed after completion).

Not proposed upstream: draft in patches/tonic-UPSTREAM-DRAFT.md, awaiting
owner review.

